            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "This follows the URI scheme specification                                (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-3.1): \r\n%a restricts the first character to a letter, while %w allows digits in subsequent      \r\ncharacters. This corresponds to the grammar ALPHA *( ALPHA / DIGIT / \"+\" / \"-\" / \".\" ).                                                               \r\n                                                                           \r\nI also looked for an existing utility function to reuse, but couldn’t find \r\none, so I inlined the check.",
            "commit_id": "2c4b8dc5c4867112b63410b436c3c36428406272",
            "created_at": "2026-07-11T12:08:54Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -3254,7 +3254,9 @@ function M.match(args)\n   end\n \n   if name then\n-    if name:sub(-1) == '/' then\n+    -- A trailing slash in a URI is part of the resource name and does not\n+    -- imply that the buffer represents a filesystem directory.\n+    if name:sub(-1) == '/' and not name:match('^%a[%w+.-]*://') then",
